  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig. 1.1.1, 'Planning and implementing a digital health enterprise: phases, steps and resources'. Seven colour-coded phases — 01 assessing the current state and enabling environment; 02 establishing a shared understanding and strategic planning; 03 defining the future state; 04 planning the enterprise architecture; 05 determining health content requirements; 06 M&E of digital health implementations and fostering data use; 07 implementing, maintaining and scaling — each with its steps. Resource tiles are placed against the phases they serve and marked PDF or online. They include the WHO Digital Health Atlas, the WHO/ITU National eHealth Strategy Toolkit, the ITU SDG Digital Investment Framework, TOGAF, Open HIE, the WHO SMART Guidelines, the WHO MAPS toolkit and the ADB Total Cost of Ownership Tool. The 'Digital implementation investment guide (this document)' tile is highlighted spanning phases 02 to 05. This chart is the original of the versions reused in later WHO handbooks.",
